/-!
# Half-critical reduction of the whole restart dual-square obstruction

The existing exact physical-window ledger says that finite accumulated time
forces the actual viscous/nonlinear `H⁻¹` square payment to be unbounded.
The half-critical whole-gradient telescope now supplies the missing upper
payment on every crossing-free prefix.

This module joins those two already generated ledgers before any frequency
or occurrence quotient.  Its terminal theorem is a genuine regularity
hard-gate reduction:

```text
finite accumulated physical time
→ some actual native current crosses the fixed half-critical threshold.
```

The crossing index is generated by the real restart run.  No branch,
critical margin, cutoff, output coordinate, or square-budget certificate is
accepted from a caller.
-/

